<title>USA: Minnesota Housing Finance Agency $32 mln priced.</title>
<headline>Minnesota Housing Finance Agency $32 mln priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $32 million of Minnesota Housing Finance Agency single-family mortgage revenue bonds, 1995 Series M (non-AMT), with a top yield of 5.875 percent in 2017.</p>
<p>MINNESOTA HOUSING FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $32,025,000*</p>
<p>SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE BONDS</p>
<p>1995 SERIES M (NON-AMT)</p>
<p>THIS IS A PRELIMINARY PRICING.</p>
<p>				REMARKETING</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa		    S&amp;P: AA+</p>
<p>    Expected		   Expected</p>
<p>DATED: 12/14/1995	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 01/01 &amp; 07/01</p>
<p>INTEREST ACCRUES: 12/12/1996</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		AMOUNT*   AMOUNT*   COUPON</p>
<p>			   (1/1)    (7/1)</p>
<p>1999		     550M	560M    4.20  %</p>
